From: Nova-Deck <novadeck@localhost>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qdsp6: q6apm-lpass-dais: start playback port at prepare

Port start moved out of .prepare and into .trigger, so the MI2S bit clock
now only comes up after the codec DAPM widgets have powered on. The aw88166
speaker amps on the AYN SM8550 boards validate their PLL against BCLK at
DAPM PRE_PMU, i.e. before the PCM trigger fires. With no clock present the
PLL never locks: the amps stay silent and each attempt retries and spams
the log, which also stretches the audio bring-up at boot.

Start the playback port back in .prepare so BCLK is running before PRE_PMU.
The !is_port_started guard in the trigger then no-ops, and the capture path
is untouched.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-lpass-dais.c
@@ -222,6 +222,20 @@
 		dev_err(dai->dev, "Failed to prepare Graph %d\n", rc);
 		goto err;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * aw88166 checks its PLL against BCLK at DAPM PRE_PMU, before the
+	 * PCM trigger; start the port here so BCLK is up in time. The
+	 * trigger's !is_port_started guard then no-ops. Playback only.
+	 */
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
+		rc = q6apm_graph_start(dai_data->graph[dai->id]);
+		if (rc < 0) {
+			dev_err(dai->dev, "Failed to start APM port %d\n", dai->id);
+			goto err;
+		}
+		dai_data->is_port_started[dai->id] = true;
+	}
 	return 0;
 err:
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
--
2.43.0
